      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day). A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. That much ibuprofen raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum for inflammatory conditions or severe pain.\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth, every 6 hours.** This is the usual dose for mild to moderate pain.\n- **1,600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg 4 times daily or 800 mg twice daily.\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though it may still need pharmacist or prescriber review. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
